WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:18.027
The next day in cooking class, Mrs.

2
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:21.528
Hag was explaining the importance of using the best ingredients.

3
00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:26.450
Ben tried to listen, but he was distracted by his worries about Winnie.

4
00:00:27.471 --> 00:00:30.112
And his worries that Winnie would know what he was thinking.

5
00:00:31.908 --> 00:00:35.532
"Everything should be moldy or rotten," Mrs.

6
00:00:35.572 --> 00:00:36.653
Hag told the students.

7
00:00:37.694 --> 00:00:41.917
"Some cooks like to use fresh earwax and pocket lint."

8
00:00:47.883 --> 00:00:52.047
Ben didn't have any earwax, so he reached into his pocket to see about lint.

9
00:00:53.668 --> 00:00:57.692
He felt the tooth he'd found in the broom flying classroom and took it out of his pocket.

10
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.623
Mrs. Hag spotted it as she walked past Ben's worktable.

11
00:01:03.643 --> 00:01:08.387
"Oh, you've got a bat claw.

12
00:01:08.927 --> 00:01:11.809
I bought some the other day, but I can't find them.

13
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.332
I guess I lost them somewhere."

14
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:17.154
Ben was stunned.

15
00:01:18.095 --> 00:01:21.477
The object in his palm wasn't a tooth; it was a bat claw!

16
00:01:22.498 --> 00:01:23.039
Had Mrs.

17
00:01:23.139 --> 00:01:26.281
Hag accidentally dropped one in the broom-flying classroom?

18
00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:34.181
Could she be Did that mean Winnie "Oh, wow," Ben murmured.

19
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:35.842
He had to tell Mr.

20
00:01:35.882 --> 00:01:41.124
Freaky! But Ben knew he needed proof before he accused a teacher of anything.

21
00:01:42.284 --> 00:01:43.325
He glanced at Mog.

22
00:01:43.945 --> 00:01:45.165
Maybe Mog would help him.

23
00:01:45.906 --> 00:01:49.807
They weren't exactly friends now, but they weren't enemies anymore either.

24
00:01:52.048 --> 00:01:54.989
At the end of the day, Ben found Mog in the hallway.

25
00:01:55.009 --> 00:01:58.631
"Mog! I need to talk to you."

26
00:01:59.691 --> 00:02:02.676
"Sure," said Mog.

27
00:02:03.216 --> 00:02:03.637
"What's up?"

28
00:02:03.657 --> 00:02:06.717
"I think Mrs.

29
00:02:06.777 --> 00:02:09.698
Hag is the one flying the brooms," whispered Ben.

30
00:02:09.718 --> 00:02:12.819
"Really?" said Mog.

31
00:02:13.619 --> 00:02:14.520
He looked shocked.

32
00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.600
Ben filled him in.

33
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:23.182
makes sense," said Mog.

34
00:02:23.202 --> 00:02:25.763
"Winnie told me Mrs.

35
00:02:25.803 --> 00:02:27.543
Hag was really upset when Mr.

36
00:02:27.603 --> 00:02:29.684
Freaky made her stop teaching broom flying.

37
00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:32.589
And everyone says she's terrible at flying.

38
00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.011
That could explain the crashing brooms."

39
00:02:36.291 --> 00:02:37.072
Ben nodded.

40
00:02:37.852 --> 00:02:40.394
He was getting more and more excited about his theory.

41
00:02:40.414 --> 00:02:42.875
"Now we just need to prove it."

42
00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:47.417
"Let's look for clues in the broom-flying classroom," said Mog.

43
00:02:49.718 --> 00:02:52.480
The two monsters hurried upstairs and into the classroom.

44
00:02:58.892 --> 00:03:00.373
"Hey!" cried a voice from the closet.

45
00:03:00.393 --> 00:03:02.193
"Get me out of here!"

46
00:03:02.213 --> 00:03:04.274
"That's Winnie!"

47
00:03:04.614 --> 00:03:05.215
cried Ben.

48
00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:08.096
He quickly unlocked the closet door.

49
00:03:08.936 --> 00:03:10.417
Winnie leaped out of the closet.

50
00:03:14.698 --> 00:03:15.699
It was hot in there!"

51
00:03:15.719 --> 00:03:19.520
"What were you doing in the broom closet?"

52
00:03:19.921 --> 00:03:20.601
asked Mog.

53
00:03:20.621 --> 00:03:24.502
"I came up here to look at the brooms," said Winnie.

54
00:03:24.522 --> 00:03:26.363
"I miss them.

55
00:03:26.823 --> 00:03:27.344
But Mrs.

56
00:03:27.424 --> 00:03:28.204
Hag was here.

57
00:03:29.432 --> 00:03:33.413
She pushed me into the closet and locked me—" Crash!

58
00:03:34.073 --> 00:03:35.794
A window smashed as Mrs.

59
00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:38.855
Hag rocketed into the room, flying two brooms.

60
00:03:38.875 --> 00:03:40.615
"Look out!"

61
00:03:41.075 --> 00:03:41.656
she cried.

62
00:03:42.676 --> 00:03:47.117
The brooms shot around the room, zipped upside down, and then flew out the door.

63
00:03:47.137 --> 00:03:51.278
Ben, Mog, and Winnie rushed into the hallway.

64
00:03:52.439 --> 00:03:54.139
One broom flew out from under Mrs.

65
00:03:54.179 --> 00:03:56.080
Hag and crashed into a trophy case.

66
00:03:57.056 --> 00:04:00.559
The teacher lost her grip on the other one, which shot up through the ceiling.

67
00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.361
Mrs. Hag tumbled downward.

68
00:04:04.562 --> 00:04:06.423
Bam! She crashed into Mr.

69
00:04:06.463 --> 00:04:21.435
Freaky. The next day Mrs.

70
00:04:21.475 --> 00:04:22.776
Hag announced her retirement.

71
00:04:26.496 --> 00:04:29.920
It turned out that she'd been making trouble at school to get back at Mr.

72
00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:36.567
Freaky. Ben didn't think anyone at Monster Academy was sorry to see Mrs.

73
00:04:36.607 --> 00:04:37.168
Hag go.

74
00:04:38.169 --> 00:04:43.515
Mr. Freaky had already hired a new cooking teacher, and Miss Bungle was going to start teaching broom

75
00:04:43.555 --> 00:04:44.176
flying again.

76
00:04:45.377 --> 00:04:47.880
Later Gaby rushed up to Ben in the hallway.

77
00:04:50.264 --> 00:04:51.125
"Did you hear the news?

78
00:04:51.585 --> 00:04:53.826
Mr. Freaky rescheduled the Monster Mash dance.

79
00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:55.087
It's tomorrow night.

80
00:04:55.507 --> 00:04:57.288
Now Waldo and I can go together.

81
00:04:57.688 --> 00:04:59.389
It's going to be so awesome!"

82
00:05:05.172 --> 00:05:07.333
Ben floated down the hallway toward his locker.

83
00:05:08.554 --> 00:05:12.456
He was glad for Gaby, but he couldn't help feeling a little sorry for himself.

84
00:05:13.737 --> 00:05:15.518
Winnie wasn't mad at Mog anymore.

85
00:05:16.398 --> 00:05:18.900
So now she would go with Mog to the dance, of course.

86
00:05:20.316 --> 00:05:22.338
"It's just as well," thought Ben.

87
00:05:23.398 --> 00:05:24.839
Mog was his friend now too.

88
00:05:25.579 --> 00:05:28.381
Maybe Ben could— "Hey, Ben!"

89
00:05:28.921 --> 00:05:30.182
shouted Mog just then.

90
00:05:31.163 --> 00:05:32.884
The monster came running toward him.

91
00:05:32.904 --> 00:05:36.506
"Hey, Mog," Ben replied.

92
00:05:36.526 --> 00:05:38.287
"Do you know Lilly?"

93
00:05:38.867 --> 00:05:39.568
asked Mog.

94
00:05:40.788 --> 00:05:42.850
"She's got three eyes and a big blue horn."

95
00:05:42.870 --> 00:05:45.551
"No," said Ben.

96
00:05:45.571 --> 00:05:52.705
"Why?" "I just asked her to the Monster Mash dance," said Mog with a big smile.

97
00:05:52.725 --> 00:05:54.986
"And she said yes!"

98
00:05:55.006 --> 00:05:57.467
"That's great!"

99
00:05:58.007 --> 00:05:58.567
said Ben.

100
00:05:58.587 --> 00:06:00.407
"But what about Winnie?

101
00:06:00.928 --> 00:06:04.108
Aren't you two—" "Nah," said Mog.

102
00:06:04.729 --> 00:06:05.429
"We broke up."

103
00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:12.351
When Mog left, Ben felt a smile spread across his face.

104
00:06:13.191 --> 00:06:14.691
Winnie and Mog had broken up!

105
00:06:15.631 --> 00:06:17.432
Now he could ask Winnie to the dance!

106
00:06:18.668 --> 00:06:22.151
But as he floated toward the exit, Ben felt himself getting nervous.

107
00:06:22.171 --> 00:06:25.614
"Maybe she won't say yes," he thought.

108
00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.236
"Maybe she's already going with someone else."

109
00:06:35.102 --> 00:06:40.047
Outside, he could see Winnie soaring over the soccer field on one of the school brooms.

110
00:06:40.927 --> 00:06:45.952
She was leaning over it with a happy look on her face, probably thrilled to be flying again.

111
00:06:50.848 --> 00:06:51.550
"Here goes."

112
00:06:52.572 --> 00:06:55.097
Ben took a deep breath and then headed toward her.
